### What are Java 17 LTS features?

Java 17 is an LTS (Long-Term Support) release that consolidates several preview features into stable APIs. It is the baseline for Spring Boot 3.x and the most widely adopted Java version in enterprise environments.

### What are records?

Records (JEP 395, final in Java 16) are immutable data carriers that eliminate POJO boilerplate.

```java
package com.bank.model;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

// One line replaces ~50 lines of POJO boilerplate
public record Trade(String tradeId, String symbol, BigDecimal amount, String status) {}

// Auto-generated: constructor, getters (tradeId(), symbol(), etc.),
// equals(), hashCode(), toString()
```

```text
Trade t = new Trade("TRD-001", "RELIANCE", new BigDecimal("245050"), "SETTLED");
t.symbol()     // "RELIANCE" (accessor, not getSymbol())
t.toString()   // Trade[tradeId=TRD-001, symbol=RELIANCE, amount=245050, status=SETTLED]
```

### What are sealed classes?

Sealed classes (JEP 409) restrict which types can extend or implement a type. This creates a closed hierarchy that the compiler can verify for exhaustiveness in switch.

```java
package com.bank.model;

import java.math.BigDecimal;

public sealed interface Instruction permits Buy, Sell, Transfer {}
public record Buy(String symbol, int qty) implements Instruction {}
public record Sell(String symbol, int qty) implements Instruction {}
public record Transfer(String from, String to, BigDecimal amount) implements Instruction {}

// Adding a new subtype without updating all switches is a compile error
```

### What is pattern matching instanceof?

Pattern matching instanceof (JEP 394) combines the type check and cast in one expression, eliminating the separate cast line.

```java
// BEFORE: separate check and cast
if (obj instanceof Trade) {
    Trade t = (Trade) obj;        // redundant cast
    process(t.amount());
}

// AFTER: combined check and binding
if (obj instanceof Trade t) {    // t is bound and cast in one step
    process(t.amount());
}

// Works with negation too:
if (!(obj instanceof Trade t)) {
    return;  // not a Trade
}
process(t.amount());  // t is in scope here
```

### How do records, sealed, and pattern matching work together?

```java
public String describe(Instruction instr) {
    return switch (instr) {
        case Buy b     -> "Buy " + b.qty() + " of " + b.symbol();
        case Sell s    -> "Sell " + s.qty() + " of " + s.symbol();
        case Transfer t -> "Transfer Rs." + t.amount() + " from " + t.from() + " to " + t.to();
        // Exhaustive: all permitted subtypes covered
    };
}
```

This gives Java algebraic-data-type modeling: a sealed hierarchy of records with exhaustive pattern matching.

### How is Java 17 different from Java 8?

| Feature | Java 8 | Java 17 |
|---|---|---|
| Data carriers | Verbose POJOs | Records |
| Type hierarchies | Open (any class can extend) | Sealed (controlled) |
| Type checking | instanceof + cast | Pattern matching instanceof |
| Switch | Statement, fall-through | Expression, no fall-through |
| Multi-line strings | String concatenation | Text blocks |
| Modules | Not available | Available (since Java 9) |
| GC | Parallel GC default | G1 GC default, ZGC available |

### Why do teams adopt Java 17?

- Spring Boot 3.x requires Java 17 as minimum. Spring Boot 2.x reached end-of-life in November 2023.
- LTS: Oracle and vendors provide security patches for years (minimum 5 years, extended support longer).
- Modern features reduce boilerplate and bugs (records, sealed, pattern matching).
- Performance: improved GC (G1, ZGC), better JIT compilation, and startup improvements.
- The upgrade path from Java 11 is smooth for most applications.

### What should a senior engineer know?

- Strong encapsulation of JDK internals means `--add-opens` may be needed for libraries that use deep reflection (Hibernate, Mockito older versions).
- Records are implicitly `final` and cannot extend classes (but can implement interfaces).
- Sealed classes and records together replace the Visitor pattern with simpler exhaustive switch.
- Java 17 removed deprecated APIs: RMI Activation, Applet API, and Security Manager (for removal).

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

- Can a record have custom methods? (Yes. You can add instance methods, static methods, and compact constructors for validation.)
- Can a sealed class have non-sealed subtypes? (Yes. A `non-sealed` subtype reopens the hierarchy for extension.)
- What is the next LTS after Java 17? (Java 21, released September 2023.)
